# josh-proxy filter spec — monorepo ⇄ per-actor public mirrors (ADR-2606231200).
#
# josh (https://github.com/josh-project/josh) serves *virtual* git views of this
# monorepo over a thin proxy: a clone of a filtered view is a normal git repo,
# and pushes back through the proxy land in the right monorepo subtree. This is
# the bidirectional upgrade of `git subtree split` (one-way) and avoids the
# submodule-pointer-sync blowup at 59→1245 actors.
#
# A per-actor public mirror = the subdirectory filter on its prefix:
#
#   :/20-actors/<name>
#
# Clone a single actor's view (read or PR-write) via the running proxy:
#
#   git clone http://localhost:8002/etzhayyim/root.git:/20-actors/cargo.git \
#             com-etzhayyim-cargo
#
# Workspace form (a curated multi-actor view) — declare prefixes here and clone
# the whole workspace as one repo with each actor at its own top-level dir:

cargo  = :/20-actors/cargo
vessel = :/20-actors/vessel
port   = :/20-actors/port

# Add one line per actor as it graduates from the pilot. The `actor:publish`
# task seeds/refreshes each mirror branch; josh-proxy is what makes the view
# writable (PRs on com-etzhayyim-<name> flow back to 20-actors/<name>).
